 "result": "All of this is in `src/tessel/views.py`.\n\n**Building the view function: `View.to_view_func` (L86)**\n- It's a classmethod. It defines an inner `view(**kwargs)` function that instantiates the class (once per request by default, or once up front if `init_every_request` is `False`).\n- It then calls `active_app.ensure_sync(self.run_view)(**kwargs)`.\n- It attaches `view_class`, `__name__`, `methods` and `provide_automatic_options` to the function, and wraps it in any `decorators`.\n- You pass the result to `attach_route_rule(..., view_func=...)`, which reads `view.methods` to decide which HTTP methods the rule accepts.\n\n**Choosing the allowed methods: `VerbView.__init_subclass__` (L165)**\n- When the class is defined, it sets `cls.methods` unless the class declares `methods` itself.\n- It starts from the `methods` of the base classes.\n- It then adds the upper-cased name of each entry in `http_method_funcs` that the class has, so `get()` and `post()` become `{\"GET\", \"POST\"}`.\n\n**Dispatching per request: `VerbView.run_view` (L182)**\n- It looks up `getattr(self, request.method.lower())` and calls it with the URL kwargs, via `ensure_sync`.\n- A `HEAD` request with no `head()` falls back to `get()`.\n- If there is no handler, an assertion fails with \"Unimplemented method\".\n\n`View.run_view` (L78) is the abstract hook that raises `NotImplementedError`. `VerbView` overrides it with the dispatcher above.",
